  "text_to_speech": "[Music] this past spring I had the pleasure of hike in the Grand Champion trail from picket post Mountain to Albuquerque and for the potential benefit of future hikers I thought I'd put together a quick and dirty guide to aspects of the trail in descending order of importance first and foremost is worth considering the season of travel I chose to hike in the spring of a wet winter and as such water was great but any spring time through hike of the granite in the trail will involve going through the moji on mountains in the Gila country sometime in March or April and according to the u.s. Forest Service average nighttime temperatures have 5600 feet Gila Hot Springs is 25 degrees in April so check the weather and pack accordingly secondly navigation seems to be a concern for the Grande enchanted Trail because it's a route and not a officially designated trail and so the use of some navigational tool is pretty much essential I benefited from using a dedicated Garmin GPS device as well as a smartphone with backcountry navigator if one device failed usually the other device did not fail at the same time so I always had a navigational redundancy they're also a few town concerns to be aware of is worth noting that all of the Arizona Trail towns are in the copper corridor which is a productive mining district in southern Arizona and as such the hotels in these trail towns have a tendency to fill up with seasonal mine workers so if you can call ahead for hotel rooms it's probably not a bad idea I had the pleasure of meeting 12 other thru-hikers in the two months that I was on the g-e-t and I did end up doing a lot of solo hiking before I bumped into some other travelers so it's worth considering that if you would like company on your hike you may consider talking a friend into through hiking it with you also trail conditions change in the backcountry sometimes unexpectedly and frequently so it's good to have an adventurous attitude while also hiking smart bottom line don't take my word for it [Music] you",
